# Permanent redirects for the URLs the prototype shipped.
#
# The prototype served .html files. Anything already linked to them — including
# anything a publication printed — must keep working, so these are 301s and they
# are permanent commitments.
#
# Read by both Netlify and Cloudflare Pages, same format. First match wins,
# which is why these sit here rather than being appended: tools/redirects.mjs
# adds the per-project rules and the CMS's own redirects to dist/_redirects
# after the build, below these.
#
# Written one rule per line rather than as a pattern. The pattern version —
# /projects/:slug.html — does not mean what it looks like: a placeholder cannot
# carry a suffix inside a segment, so it matched EVERY path under /projects/ and
# sent it to the literal string "/projects/:slug/". Every project page on the
# live site became a redirect loop. Explicit rules cannot do that.

/index.html      /            301
/projects.html   /projects/   301
/studio.html     /studio/     301
/people.html     /people/     301
/press.html      /press/      301
/contact.html    /contact/    301
